Proposed score: 1.25 of 2.5, for partial alignment. The only water planning document on the Citation Sheet is the November 2017 JICA Final Report for BWSSB's Bengaluru Water Supply and Sewerage Project (Phase 3). It refers to BDA's Master Plan 2015, the statutory plan under the Karnataka Town and Country Planning (KTCP) Act. It reproduces that plan's proposed land-use map (Figure 2.4.2) and describes the Vision 2015 framework, which marks out where development is to be focused. It also takes the Master Plan 2015 annual growth rate of 0.78% for the Core area as an input to its population projections. These projections drive water demand and the sizing of the Stage V water project and of sewage volumes by zone.

The report does not show that the master plan's growth areas or land-use zones decided where the network expands or where major facilities go. Sewerage systems were laid out using 'Topographic conditions', 'Planned location of STP site and land availability' and the option of merging with neighbouring systems. Population was projected for administrative areas (Core, ULBs, 110 Villages), not master-plan zones. The density figures it uses come from 'Draft Master Planning Criteria' (May 2016), which appear to belong to BWSSB's own draft water and sewerage master plan, not the BDA plan.

